"### Regulatory outlook\n\n**Where it stands (facts):**\n- Hyperliquid is **offshore and geoblocks US users**; it holds no US license and raised no VC \u2014 a deliberately arms-length structure.\n- It lists **equity/index/commodity perps** (SP500, NVDA, GOLD\u2026) via HIP-3 builders \u2014 instruments that in the US are **securities/commodity derivatives** under SEC/CFTC purview.\n- The **JELLY incident (Mar 2025)** showed validators can intervene in markets by vote \u2014 a governance fact regulators and users both weigh.\n\n**The swing factors (open \u2014 flag as uncertain \ud83d\udd35):**\n- \ud83d\udd35 A US **market-structure / 'CLARITY'-type act** giving DeFi legal certainty would be a *re-rating* event (analysts model the regulatory risk premium collapsing \u2192 higher fair value).\n- \ud83d\udd35 Conversely, **CFTC/SEC action** on on-chain derivatives \u2014 or CME/ICE lobbying against tokenised equity perps \u2014 is the primary tail risk; geoblocking reduces but doesn't remove exposure.\n- \ud83d\udd35 **Stablecoin regulation** now matters directly to revenue after the **Coinbase/USDC** migration (collateral-yield stream).\n\n**How to watch it:** the reg-arb that powers the RWA growth story (see Competitive Landscape) is the same surface that attracts enforcement. Treat regulatory clarity as the biggest *two-sided* catalyst for HYPE \u2014 upside if it legitimises, downside if it constrains.\n\n<sub>Synthesis of official docs + reporting; \ud83d\udd35 = community/analyst expectation, not settled law. Not legal or investment advice.</sub>"